    <h1>Thick-billed Raven Range: Where This Species Lives</h1>
  </header>

  <section class="qa-snippet" aria-label="Direct answer">
    <p><strong class="claim-science">[science]</strong> The Thick-billed Raven (<em>Corvus crassirostris</em>) is essentially endemic to the Ethiopian Highlands, with range extensions into Eritrea, northern Somalia, and Djibouti. It is confined to highland and montane habitats above approximately 1,500 m and is the dominant large corvid throughout Ethiopia. It is one of the most restricted-range ravens — essentially a Highland Ethiopian bird.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="qa-section">
    <h2>Distribution</h2>
    <p><strong class="claim-science">[science]</strong> The Thick-billed Raven's range is tightly centred on the Ethiopian Highlands:<sup><a href="#src-1">1</a></sup></p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Ethiopia:</strong> present throughout the highlands — both the northern highlands (Tigray, Amhara, Afar highlands) and the southern highlands (Oromia, SNNPR). Common in highland cities (Addis Ababa, Gondar, Bahir Dar, Lalibela) and rural highland areas. Abundant in the Simien and Bale Mountain ranges.</li>
      <li><strong>Eritrea:</strong> present in the highland plateau regions of central Eritrea (around Asmara and the escarpment) — the northern extension of the Ethiopian Highlands.</li>
      <li><strong>Somalia (northern) and Djibouti:</strong> the northern Somali highlands (around Hargeisa, in Somaliland) have some records, as does Djibouti in upland areas — these represent the southeastern fringe of the range.</li>
      <li><strong>Elevation:</strong> primarily 1,500–4,000 m. Most abundant at 2,000–3,500 m — the highland plateau zone.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The species is essentially absent from lowland Ethiopia (Afar Depression, Ogaden, Omo lowlands) and from all countries outside the Ethiopian/Eritrean highlands.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="qa-section">
    <h2>Habitat</h2>
    <p><strong class="claim-science">[science]</strong> Within its highland range, the Thick-billed Raven uses a variety of open and semi-open habitats:<sup><a href="#src-1">1</a></sup></p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cliffs and gorges:</strong> the primary nest habitat — steep basaltic cliff faces in highland gorges (the Blue Nile/Abbay gorge, the Rift Valley escarpment, the Simien escarpment) provide nesting sites.</li>
      <li><strong>Open highland:</strong> moorland, highland grassland, Afroalpine heathland at higher elevations; forages extensively in open terrain.</li>
      <li><strong>Agricultural and urban:</strong> very tolerant of human presence; common on highland farms, roadsides, rubbish dumps, and in towns. This adaptability has made it a familiar bird throughout settled highland Ethiopia.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

